# dev/ IS TRACKED, deliberately — do not add it here.
#
# It holds the test suites and dev/AI-README.md, and for one release they
# lived only on the owner's machine: not in git, not on GitHub, one disk
# failure from gone. The brief is also the only record of why anything in
# this project is the way it is, so it has to travel WITH the project.
#
# Keeping it out of the running container is `.dockerignore`'s job, not
# this file's. The repo and the image are different things: `git pull`
# puts dev/ on the NAS, and the Docker build then ignores it.
